<title>JAPAN: Japan 96/97 first half c/a surplus down 35.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan 96/97 first half c/a surplus down 35.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's current account, the broadest measure of trade in goods and services, shrank 35.3 percent in the first half of 1996/97 to September 30 from a year earlier to 3.33 trillion yen, the Finance Ministry announced on Monday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the balance of payments figures follows:</p>
<p>(Unadjusted, in yen)  APR-SEPT	  YEAR AGO</p>
<p>  Current Acct Balance+3.332 trln     +5.149 trln</p>
<p> -Goods and Services  +692.4 bln	+3.483 trln</p>
<p>     Trade Balance    +4.155 trln     +6.119 trln</p>
<p>	 Exports	  21.276 trln     19.649 trln</p>
<p>	 Imports	  17.120 trln     13.529 trln</p>
<p>   Services Balance   -3.462 trln     -2.635 trln</p>
<p> -Income Balance	+3.063 trln     +2.007 trln</p>
<p> -Current Transfers    -424.1 bln	-341.7 bln</p>
<p>(Adjusted, in yen)   APR-SEPT     YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Current Account Balance+3.681 trln    +3.953 trln</p>
<p> -Goods and Services    +991.9  bln    +2.064 trln</p>
<p>    Trade Balance	 +4.387 trln   +5.129  trln</p>
<p>	 Exports	   +21.651 trln   +20.953 trln</p>
<p>	 Imports	   +17.263 trln   +15.823 trln</p>
<p>    Services Balance    -3.395 trln    -3.065 trln</p>
<p> -Income Balance	  +3.141 trln    +2.370 trln</p>
<p> -Current Transfers	-451.8 bln     -481.7 bln</p>
<p>The following figures show the unadjusted balance in Japan's capital and financial accounts (in yen):</p>
<p>			    APR-SEPT     YEAR AGO</p>
<p>Capital/Financial Acct -1.285 trln  -1.098 trln  -Financial Account    -1.141 trln  -1.028 trln</p>
<p>  Direct Investment    -1.312 trln  -798.7 bln</p>
<p>Portfolio Investment  -771.0 bln  -3.777 trln   Other Investment	+942.6 bln  +3.548 trln</p>
<p> -Capital Account	 -144.8 bln    -70.4 bln</p>
